  message: "MEASUREMENTS THAT RESHAPE THIS ITEM (from the 08-16 01:00 UTC full-suite\ncron log at 8b55d1f4ef, fetched with the WI-zavut log tool):\n\n1. THE \"3.10-ONLY\" HYPOTHESIS IS DEAD. The full-suite container is Python\n   3.11.14 and fails the same test the same way. Not interpreter-versioned\n   in the way filed.\n\n2. THE FAILURE IS NARROWER THAN FILED. The test's FIRST assertion (the\n   pyproject script file-node survives the noise filter with entry_point\n   set) PASSES in CI — the log's failure is `assert []` on the SECOND\n   (entrypoints list). So the file-role path works; what is missing in CI\n   is the toml_config SYMBOL-concept -> entrypoints.py derivation\n   (concept_type == \"pyproject_script\" -> CLI_COMMAND/manifest_declared).\n   The gap is in that chain, under CI conditions only.\n\n3. ENVIRONMENT AXES ELIMINATED from the failing run's own install log:\n   tree-sitter-toml 0.7.0 present; tree-sitter 0.25.2 identical to the\n   local (passing) box. Grammar availability and library versions are not\n   the axis.\n\n4. TREE WINDOW. The failing tree 8b55d1f4ef is an ancestor of 4e8c47e47d,\n   where the nightly matrix passes the full suite on ALL of 3.10-3.13. The\n   window contains only PRs #364/#365/#366 — none touching toml_config.py\n   or entrypoints.py. The failure therefore stopped expressing WITHOUT its\n   mechanism being fixed. Leading hypothesis: pytest-xdist\n   ordering/collection shift (the climb PRs added tests, redistributing\n   workers) — i.e. an inter-test interaction expressed only under CI's\n   worker layout. Treat as LATENT.\n\n5. REPRO CONSTRAINTS, stated: local single-test and whole-file runs pass\n   (3.12, xdist and single-process); this box cannot run the 3.11\n   container (agent user not in the docker group). The failure has only\n   ever been observed under CI's full-suite worker layout.\n\nNEXT LEVERS, in rough order of information-per-cost: (a) INV-libib — until\nthe four nightly leg logs stop collapsing, per-leg attribution stays\nunmeasurable; (b) a CI-side probe: run test_run_behavior_map.py FIRST /\nisolated in the cron (or -p no:randomly single-worker) to split\n\"environment\" from \"ordering\"; (c) docker-group access for a faithful\ncontainer repro. Do NOT close on the current green — that is\nnon-reproduction, not evidence."  # 6cb1
